posal costs a missed clock, while a promoted fuzzy one corrupts the record. The pattern's BECAUSE ('preserves provenance and enables explicit promotion') is why the mention is kept rather than dropped: it stays diagnosable, and an explicit rule can promote it later.", :response-id "response-9d4c94d8991db9be", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385106862-24586-61928648"}}, :process/spec-drift-by-displacement {:request-id "request-4a8559ab33b4b7c2", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/process/spec-drift-by-displacement.flexiarg", :sha256 "7b41395c3703ff5bdc288c85fdbb2b1746438294cdef82594a568b75b97b2edd"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern concerns plans and specifications being displaced by newer artifacts, and its receipts (DRIFT-2026-09-05, the APM park-sink vocabulary) do not carry over. What carries over is the principle: only an authored decision may replace the source of truth, applied here to a runtime value rather than a document. The pattern does not decide that the operator is the author of the clock and bell senders are not; the mission does (Joe 2026-06-03, claude-8 2026-09-24). Explicit dispatch --mission is also an authored decision, and INSTANTIATE-5 keeps it authoritative. The amendment's 'dispatch turn never switches' can therefore only cover prose mentions in a dispatched prompt, and no test covers that case yet.", :want :exit/h64ddcd0e8811, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of