cit-promotion-to-facts] :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts}, :missing-meets [], :precedence-violations []}, :stopped-is-not-success true, :target "M-autoclock-in", :family-searched 2, :budget-used 1}}, :at "2026-09-26T01:13:13.753764210Z"}, :reading "Same interpretation as my earlier answer for this token; the pattern bytes are unchanged. The amendment divides turns by who wrote them, and the pattern says why that division is right: 'nothing replaces a typed source of truth without an author-authored decision', enforced by a boundary that refuses anything else, separating a decision from a mere change. The session's clock is a typed source of truth: turn→mission attribution that other work builds on. An operator turn naming an exact target is an author-authored decision, because the operator holds the clock, can see it, and is changing it. So the resolver switches (exact-mention-overrides-stale-clock-and-refusals-keep-it). A bell, auto-bellback or dispatch-prose mention is displacement: the clock would be replaced without any actor deciding to replace it. That is what happened when bellbacks mentioning M-futon-seams kept moving a seat's E-cascade-real clock. The refusing boundary is what bell-mentions-fill-an-empty-clock-but-do-not-switch pins: an empty clock may be filled, an occupied one is never switched. It also covers 'an ambiguous or unresolvable name records its refusal and leaves the clock where it was', since that refusal is itself recorded as a decision (kept-because). The pattern's T2a (drift goes where the checker has no jurisdiction) points at the Consequence paragraph: the Emacs buffer is outside the resolver's jurisdiction and still applies the old floor-only rule to operator input.", :response-id "response-f7d6b56cb137b171", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790385174034-24587-deaf9fa2"}}, :hygiene/observe-the-authority {:request-id "request-69bbac2e9ce5cf1d", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/hygiene/observe-the-authority.flexiarg", :sha256 "f43c2229b97e9162b4b62af0093f5d15854423b1fc810cd0da4ccdc5ed568bef"}, :kind :machine-requested, :scope-limit "The pattern's own settings (buffer cleaning, repository hygiene, test-registry environments) do not carry over, and neither does its instruction to 'emit raw signals'. What carries over is the general move of reading the authority instead of trusting the stand-in. The ERT test checks that the buffer adopts the returned decision. It does not re-check the resolver, which clock-decision-test covers. The pattern also does not choose which side is the authority; the mission's amendment makes that choice.", :want :exit/h203ce9577ebe, :by "claude-5", :validated {:checks [:canonical-id :library-source-sha :produces-want :guard-tokens-known :owner-constraints :constructs-through-it :admitted], :candidate {:precedence [:orchestration/pattern-warranted-choice-point :sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts :process/spec-drift-by-displacement :hygiene/observe-the-authority :sidecar/proposal-ledger-for-fuzzy-output], :construction-receipt {:locator-coverage :token-set-not-supplied, :unknown-read-as-not-established [], :g-of-best {:value 22.99316913014941, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :moves [{:move-id :compose-by-need, :value 1.25, :g-comparison {:delta 1.25, :universe [:exit/h0c55648e57e5 :exit/h0f3acdf222d7 :exit/h1dae607747ce :exit/h203ce9577ebe :exit/h59adca2cd730 :exit/h5c6933e5e2fc :exit/h64ddcd0e8811 :exit/h7afd70f40a29]}, :parts {:pragmatic 1.25, :epistemic nil, :epistemic-added 0.0, :cost 0.0, :includes-unformalised-novelty false}}], :unreached-wants [{:token :exit/h0c55648e57e5, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h0f3acdf222d7, :reason :no-producer} {:token :exit/h59adca2cd730, :reason 