4b violation. Not established with the search trail is a finding; absent without a search is an inference. Its BECAUSE: acting on silence converts an unknown into a false known. The criterion applies this rule to clock inference. An :unclocked decision is an absence claim, and it is a finding only if it carries its search. That is why each decision must record the considered sources and relevant provenance together with agent, exact session, turn/job id and time. The pattern also separates a search that ran and found nothing from a search that could not run. The criterion names the same split: Distinguish a known absence from an unavailable dependency. Every source consulted and none matching is a known absence. An unreadable holes root, or an activity or store feed that throws, is not established, and needs its own reason. Folding it into :no-source would create exactly the false known the pattern warns about. The typed reasons for ambiguous candidates and for an unresolved explicit target follow the pattern's instruction to treat unspecified behaviour as a finding to route to a decision, not as a licence. Do not silently preserve a stale unrelated target or invent a mission covers both halves of the pair. Inventing a mission lets unspecified behaviour accrete (T4a). Silently keeping a stale target reads silence as consent to the old clock. The resolver has no unavailable-evidence reason today, so the criterion reads false. Its locator is futon3c.agency.clock-decision-reasons-test, which is not yet written.", :response-id "response-363c69f83c37109a", :answered-by {:seat "claude-5", :job-id "invoke-1790389067129-24632-68e02385"}}, :apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure {:request-id "request-e2e7978b74b4aa5a", :validator {:ns "futon2.aif.want-interpretation", :source-sha256 "8cfadab5696338e1c258dd64f4c21bf2c2206614283d428bd8bfb2a5868cbaa4"}, :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/success-must-not-resemble-failure.flexiarg", :sha256 "5dce45ef7c2d1e4c8221d1a215